From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: env-gated reserve on UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Experimental knockout probe for the nondeterministic
crash tracked at llvm/llvm-project#191361.

malloc_history on an assertions build shows Sema's
UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache bucket array being freed by
DenseMap::grow()'s moveFrom() from inside a *nested*
ConstraintSatisfactionChecker::Evaluate(), while outer Evaluate frames
are still live, and the freed range subsequently being reused for an
ASTContext BumpPtrAllocator slab. Anything holding a pointer or
reference into the bucket storage across that nested insert is left
dangling.

Pre-sizing the cache means grow() never fires mid-compile, removing
that specific mechanism without perturbing the allocator globally
(unlike scribble-on-free, which suppresses the crash but changes
everything).

The env var keeps control and treatment on one binary:
  unset                              -> stock behaviour (control)
  CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE=1   -> default reserve of 1<<17 entries
  CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE=N   -> reserve N entries

The observed freed bucket array was ~1.3 MiB, so 1<<17 entries is
generous; if crashes persist, raise N before concluding the cache is
exonerated.

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of
the llvm-project monorepo, to match this repo's clang derivation's
sourceRoot (clang-src-.../clang).
---
diff --git a/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp b/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp
index 5a7dfb1..ee55507 100644
--- a/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp
+++ b/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 #include "llvm/ADT/SetVector.h"
 #include "llvm/ADT/SmallPtrSet.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/TimeProfiler.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <optional>
 
 using namespace clang;
@@ -358,6 +359,26 @@ Sema::Sema(Preprocessor &pp, ASTContext &ctxt, ASTConsumer &consumer,
   SemaPPCallbackHandler->set(*this);
 
   CurFPFeatures.setFPEvalMethod(PP.getCurrentFPEvalMethod());
+
+  // DIAGNOSTIC HOOK (downstream patch, not for upstream).
+  //
+  // Pre-size UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache so that DenseMap::grow()
+  // never runs after this point. A rehash from inside a nested
+  // ConstraintSatisfactionChecker::Evaluate() frees the old bucket array while
+  // outer Evaluate frames are still running; the freed range is later reused
+  // for ASTContext bump-allocator slabs. Reserving up front removes that
+  // mechanism and nothing else.
+  //
+  // Gated on an env var so control and treatment runs share one binary:
+  //   unset -> stock behaviour
+  //   set   -> reserve (value parsed as an entry count; 0/garbage -> 1<<17)
+  if (const char *Env = std::getenv("CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE")) {
+    unsigned long Entries = std::strtoul(Env, nullptr, 10);
+    if (Entries == 0)
+      Entries = 1ul << 17;
+    UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache.reserve(
+        static_cast<unsigned>(Entries));
+  }
 }
 
 // Anchor Sema's type info to this TU.
